📊 E-Commerce Analytics Project – Brazilian Public Dataset
This project focuses on building a complete end-to-end data analysis solution for a Brazilian e-commerce dataset. The workflow includes:

Database Construction: CSV files were imported into Microsoft SQL Server, where the data types were cleaned and standardized. Appropriate primary and foreign keys were assigned to establish relational integrity.

Data Modeling: A relational model diagram was created to visualize and understand the structure of the data.

SQL Views for Analysis: SQL views were developed to aggregate and transform the data for specific business insights, covering areas such as sales performance, customer satisfaction, delivery efficiency, and payment methods.

Power BI Integration: The views were imported into Power BI, where a comprehensive data model was built. Interactive dashboards were designed to answer key business questions and highlight actionable insights.

This project demonstrates the full pipeline from raw data to insightful visual analytics, showcasing best practices in data engineering and business intelligence.
